  "body": "## What changed\n\nA cross (radial) drill is judged against the finished part, the way the axial drill already is (`drilling::axial_warnings`).\n\n- New `operation/cross_part.rs`: `part_clear()` sweeps the finished chain through the part solid with the solid law (`verify::solid_hits`). Each move is swept along its tool axis with the point cone, shank and holder, within GOUGE_TOL. A hit refuses the op by name. Bisection finds the tip depth at first contact: under one drill radius reads \"the model has no hole there\", deeper reads \"the drill runs past the modelled hole's floor\".\n- It's called at both return points of `cross_spindle::cross_drill`, in world coordinates, after the reach, holder and rapid checks. It refuses at generation, so nothing reaches the post.\n- Fixtures: 22 existing tests drilled bars that had no modelled hole, so the check was right and the fixtures were wrong. The new helper `tests/punched_bar` models real holes:\n  - The bar is lengthened to z -80..20, with the top kept at z20. On the old r10 × 40 bar, any modelled cross hole tipped the lathe axis fit into \"every axis fits\". That's filed as #152.\n  - Each modelled hole gets an undrilled mirror hole, so the axis fit doesn't lean past the spindle law's 0.0005 mm (the #116 band). Two holes that meet on one line become one through hole.\n  - The mesh is coarser, so every suite stays under 20 s.\n  - Off-centre holes the bar can't hold run over a small core, and `drilling_cross_box`'s on-line lump is split into four corner lumps. Both are recorded in RECOMMENDED.md.\n  - No asserted number in any existing suite changed.\n\n## Pins (`drilling_cross_part`)\n\n- `a_cross_drill_into_a_solid_bar_is_refused_by_name`: generates on main\n- `a_cross_hole_deeper_than_the_modelled_hole_is_refused`: generates on main\n- `a_cross_hole_matching_its_modelled_hole_is_clean`\n\n## Readings\n\nGreen (debug):\n- Cross drilling: drilling_cross 9, _box 7, _part 3, _rapids 2, _spindle 6, _stock 8; lathe_cross_drill 4; stitch_cross 6.\n- Other drilling: drill_reach 6, drill_reach_fit 3, drill_prior 10, drill_prior_kinds 4, drill_rplane 8, drilling_axial 7, blind_floor 6, center_cut_owed 3, solid_law 4.\n- Everything else: machine 32, lathe_post 5, lathe_spindle_fit 3, lathe_spindle_law 8, posting 17, operations 117.\n\nClippy on app is clean.\n\nChangelog: A cross (radial) drill is judged against the finished part: a hole the model does not have, or one drilled past the modelled hole's floor, is refused by name and never posts\n\nFixes #117\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
